- 036 merge workspace files (`worklist.md`, `baseline-file-counts.txt`, `prompt-w1a/b.md`, `brief-w1a/b.md`) — classed `other-exception` (merge workspace) rather than `md-rewrite`; they are the census's own records.
- `.git/COMMIT_EDITMSG:32` — classed `ledger-artifact-leave` by judgment (git-internal bytes must not change).
- Residual: the whole-`review/` 049 pass truncated at 50KB; lineage counts come from per-lineage scoped passes and are observed-hit counts. Any unseen review file still moves untouched with the tree (ledger).
- `049/review/fanout-attribution.md`, `reviewed-files.txt`, `*.err` — verified 0 slug hits (not exceptions; noted for completeness).

## 4. Method line

Searches run: per-slug and combined 5-slug sweeps (`046-`…`050-` slugs) scoped to each of the five packet trees, 036, 037, `z_archive`, parent `description.json`/`graph-metadata.json`; `specs` with glob `!**/system-deep-loop/**`; per-track sweeps (`agents`, `cli-external-orchestration` incl. 071/073, `sk-communication/006`, `sk-doc`, `system-speckit`, and root-level non-specs with `!specs/**`); `.skilled`, `.git`, `.pi`, `.claude`, `.codex`, `.cursor`, `.devin`, `.hermes`, `repo-rules`, `.github`, `barter`, `a_nobel_en_zn`, root `*.md`/`*.json`, both frontmatter manifests; variant greps `\.skilled/specs/…`, `\.opencode/specs/…`, `Public/specs/…`; 049 file-type passes `**/*.md`, `**/*.json`, `**/*.jsonl`, `**/*.frame`, `**/logs/**`, `**/*.err`, `**/*.txt`, `**/*.lock`, plus `!**/review/**` and `**/review/**`; per-lineage scoped passes for wave1-glm/wave1-deepseek/wave2-glm/wave2-deepseek/swe2; containment finds `**/containment/**/system-deep-loop/<slug>/**` for all five slugs; cross-scope checks of 041–045 slugs inside the five trees and vice versa.

